  <body>
    <div class="page">
      <header>
        <span class="mark">HRWILLMOTT</span>
        <button
          class="company-shape"
          type="button"
          data-company-shape
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-controls="legal-stamp"
          title="Legally speaking?"
        >Dutch company-shaped object</button>
        <span class="legal-stamp" id="legal-stamp" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden>LEGALLY SPEAKING: YES</span>
      </header>

      <main>
        <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
          <p class="eyebrow">Official-ish internet cupboard</p>
          <h1 id="hero-title">Not a startup.</h1>
          <p class="joke">
            HRWILLMOTT is mostly here so accountants, clients, forms, robots, and mildly suspicious institutions can agree that Henry Willmott exists.
          </p>
          <p class="joke">
            Currently building things, climbing things, moving things around, and resisting the urge to turn every domain name into a business model.
          </p>
          <div class="actions" aria-label="Useful links">
            <a class="button" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/henrywillmott/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>
            <button class="button" type="button" data-open-contact>Contact</button>
          </div>
          <p class="current-status"><strong>CURRENTLY:</strong> somewhere between a spreadsheet and a steel boat.</p>
        </section>

        <details class="panel departments">
          <summary>Departments, apparently</summary>
          <p>One Dutch company. Several unrelated-looking reasons to own work trousers.</p>
          <div class="department-list">
            <details class="department">
              <summary>Rope access</summary>
              <p>Industrial work performed in places that would benefit from a floor.</p>
            </details>
            <details class="department">
              <summary>Software and strange internet objects</summary>
              <p>Small operational tools built because the spreadsheet had become sentient.</p>
            </details>
            <details class="department">
              <summary>Events and DJ things</summary>
              <p>Music, facilitation, production, and the occasional controlled loss of professionalism.</p>
            </details>
            <details class="department">
              <summary>Boats and maritime schemes</summary>
              <p>A steel boat, an unreasonable number of plans, and cautious use of the word “seaworthy.”</p>
            </details>
            <details class="department">
              <summary>Administrative survival</summary>
              <p>Invoices sent, forms completed, receipts located. Eventually.</p>
            </details>
          </div>
        </details>

